From 852da274f6fb8875e33c290bfbf426d5f94a5f10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: p1neappleXpress <p1ne@openflux.local>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 09:50:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(exit): SOCKS5 UDP with credentials, IPv6/domain
 relays and a real test

- carry proxy user/password into UDP ASSOCIATE (RFC 1929), so exits with
  --upstream-proxy socks5://user:pass@host keep UDP working;
- parse the associate reply by ATYP (IPv4/IPv6/domain) instead of assuming 10 bytes;
- encode the destination as IPv4/IPv6/domain, not IPv4 only;
- deadline the SOCKS handshake so a stalled proxy cannot hang a UDP flow;
- say in the log whether UDP really goes through the relay or leaves directly;
- replace the skip-unless-a-proxy-exists test with an in-process fake SOCKS5
  server covering no-auth, auth and a wrong password.
